# Story dist-2.3c. `docs/migration/` is in package.json `files[]` because CHANGELOG.md links the
# migration guide twice and it is the single most useful page an upgrading npm reader can follow
# (ADR-002 Class 3). Nothing else under `docs/` is operator-facing.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NEEDED AT ALL. npm keeps `README.md` in any directory it walks, so listing ANY
# path under `docs/` also ships `docs/README.md` — verified by controlled experiment 2026-09-07:
# with no `docs/` entry npm ships nothing here; with `docs/migration/` it ships the guide AND
# `docs/README.md`; with the named file `docs/migration/3.x-to-4.0.md` it ALSO ships
# `docs/README.md`, so narrowing the entry does not help. That file carries 7 relative links into
# repository-only siblings (agents.md, development.md, testing.md, references.md, faq.md,
# BMAD-METHOD-COMPATIBILITY.md, ../project-context.md), every one of which becomes a broken
# shipped link the moment it enters the package.
#
# WHY HERE AND NOT A `!` NEGATION IN `files[]`. Same reasoning as
# scripts/migration/format-conversion/.npmignore, which see: a negation puts a glob metacharacter
# into `files[]`, and scripts/audit/lib/installed-tree.js parses that array to build the expected
# set of `_bmad/bme/*` modules. Excluding from inside the directory needs no pattern in `files[]`,
# so that interaction does not arise. (A root `.npmignore` does NOT work when `files[]` is
# present — it must live here.)
#
# SCOPED, NOT `*`. The format-conversion file excludes everything because none of that directory
# ships. Here exactly one file must be kept out, and `docs/migration/` must still ship, so this
# names the file rather than excluding the tree.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is load-bearing. `.npmignore` uses gitignore matching, so
# a bare `README.md` matches at ANY depth below this file — it would also silently drop a future
# `docs/migration/README.md`, which is a legitimate content file that SHOULD ship. Round 1 review
# caught this: two layers independently created that file, packed, and watched it vanish with every
# check green. `/README.md` binds the pattern to this directory only. Verified both directions:
# `docs/README.md` still excluded, `docs/migration/README.md` ships.
#
# tests/lib/docs-packaging.test.js asserts all three halves: the guide ships, `docs/README.md` does
# not, and the exclusion does not reach into `docs/migration/`.
/README.md
